# spark in w3m -- your own AI, on your own machine (spark.forgewright.ai).
# Append this to your own ~/.w3m/keymap (and cgi_bin to ~/.w3m/config;
# the README's four install lines do both):
#
#     cat ~/.w3m/spark/keymap.spark >> ~/.w3m/keymap
#
# One key, spark's key in every app: M-s (Esc then s). The page you
# are reading is stashed and the spark page opens -- a small place,
# drawn by w3m itself, wearing spark's own S:
#
#   chat> [field]      the conversation: type, Enter, then [say] --
#                      follow-ups ride the same thread, and the page
#                      re-renders as the whole log
#   overview           a link: what does this page cover? (every line
#                      quotes the page, or an honest refusal, framed)
#   questions          a link: what does this page NOT answer? each
#                      question is a link that asks itself
#   part 1 . part 2    links, on a page past 16 kB: read one part
#   q (or :q, quit)    said to the field: back toward the page -- a
#                      quit word never reaches the model
#   B                  never mind, anywhere: B from an answer is the
#                      front room, B again is the page itself
#
# Nothing runs until you ask. Nothing leaves this machine but the
# rendered page text and your words, to the brain spark is configured
# for -- no URL, no path. Needs w3m 0.5.3 or newer and spark 1.20 or
# newer (spark ask -h answers). M-s is a suggestion (w3m's own M-s,
# save buffer, moves aside) -- edit the line to taste.
keymap M-s COMMAND "PIPE_BUF 'spark-w3m --stash'; BACK; GOTO file:///cgi-bin/spark.cgi"
